    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** leading the offensive charge. Despite facing a tough arm in Zac Gallen (4.36 xERA), **Kyle Tucker** (73.89) offers our highest efficiency score of the day, bolstered by strong park factors and a reliable middle-of-the-order slot. Close behind him, **Andy Pages** (66.95) provides an excellent secondary option against Gallen; his score benefits from an assumed #2 lineup spot, which maximizes his plate appearance volume against a pitcher who, while respectable, lacks the dominance to suppress our top bats. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.53) remains a high-floor anchor at first base, maintaining strong efficiency despite a neutral platoon matchup against Grant Holmes.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer involved **Coby Mayo**, whose 50.16 score just missed the cut. While **Coby Mayo** benefits from positive park factors, the optimizer preferred the slightly higher situational stability of **Curtis Mead** (50.87) and **Miguel Vargas** (51.73). **Sam Antonacci** (58.72) represents our best leverage play of the day; he is positioned at the top of the order against a beatable starter, and his refined xwOBA provides the statistical backing to justify his aggressive placement in the lineup. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Miguel Andujar** (48.26), who draws a difficult assignment against Cristopher S\u00e1nchez. His score is largely sustained by his platoon advantage, but the elite SP_xERA of 2.73 makes him a high-variance play that we are monitoring closely for potential late-game pinch-hit scenarios.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given that several of our core slots, specifically for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Kyle Tucker**, rely on pending lineup confirmations. We have intentionally benched **Jackson Merrill** (40.65) due to the severe platoon disadvantage against S\u00e1nchez and the restrictive ceiling imposed by the matchup. Managers should be prepared to pivot if the official lineups shift our hitters into unfavorable defensive slots or lower-order roles, as our current scoring is heavily dependent on the projected lineup spots for **Dominic Smith** and **Josh Jung**. Any significant drop in their batting order will trigger an immediate re-evaluation of their utility value versus the bench depth.",
